      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(markdown): keep IR text slicing UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`sliceMarkdownIR` uses `String.prototype.slice()` on code-unit positions to slice IR text. When the slice boundary falls in the middle of a surrogate pair (emoji, CJK supplementary character), the resulting text contains orphaned surrogates.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSurrogate pairs split by raw code-unit slicing produce invalid Unicode strings downstream, potentially corrupting rendered markdown or downstream consumers.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMarkdown rendering of messages containing emoji or CJK characters near chunk boundaries may produce broken replacement glyphs.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAll 34 existing tests pass plus the new surrogate pair safety test.\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [x] This change is backwards compatible\n- [x] This change has been tested with existing configurations\n",
        "branch": "fix/markdown-ir-utf16-slice",
